    "message": "fix(mcp): close the config-write file-system race\n\nCodeQL js/file-system-race, high, on the PR. writeJsonConfig checked\nexistsSync and then read, copied and wrote — the check could go stale\nbefore any of them, and it never established the read would succeed.\n\nSame fix view.ts already carries for this rule (#389): read straight out\nand let ENOENT mean absent, so there is no window between the check and\nthe use.\n\nNarrowing to ENOENT is the part that matters. Collapsing every read\nerror into \"absent\" sends a config we merely failed to read down the\nmkdir-and-write branch, which replaces it and leaves no `.bak` — the\ncopy only runs on the branch that read something.\n\nThe new test pins that: a write-only config (read fails, write would\nsucceed) must surface EACCES with the user's content intact. It fails\nagainst the collapsed-catch mutant and passes here. The earlier shape of\nthis test used a directory, which throws EISDIR either way and proved\nnothing.\n\n801 tests pass; knip, typecheck and lint clean.",
